Relevant columns & their potential usage  
• GEOGRAPHY_INDEX."GEO_NAME": fuzzy–match the Metro name to obtain its unique "GEO_ID".  
• GEOGRAPHY_INDEX."GEO_ID": identifier that will be reused in all fact‑tables.  
• GEOGRAPHY_RELATIONSHIPS."RELATED_GEO_ID": counties that are “Contained” in the metro; needed to roll county‑level IRS data up to the metro.  
• IRS_MIGRATION_BY_CHARACTERISTIC_ATTRIBUTES."VARIABLE": list of variable‑codes; filter for ILIKE '%Inflow%' AND ILIKE '%adjusted gross income%' AND ILIKE '%All AGI classes%'.  
• IRS_MIGRATION_BY_CHARACTERISTIC_TIMESERIES."VARIABLE","GEO_ID","DATE","VALUE": numeric inflow AGI for each geography & date (annual 12‑31).  
• FHFA_HOUSE_PRICE_ATTRIBUTES."VARIABLE": find the seasonally‑adjusted purchase‑only index (ILIKE '%purchase-only_monthly_SA%').  
• FHFA_HOUSE_PRICE_TIMESERIES."VARIABLE","GEO_ID","DATE","VALUE": monthly HPI series for the Metro.  

Typical filter conditions  
• Metro search: WHERE "GEO_NAME" ILIKE '%Phoenix%Mesa%Scottsdale%'.  
• Relationship: WHERE "GEO_ID" = '<Phoenix_GEO_ID>' AND "RELATIONSHIP_TYPE" = 'Contains' AND "RELATED_LEVEL" = 'County'.  
• IRS date: "DATE" IN ('2022‑12‑31','2023‑12‑31').  
• HPI dates: "DATE" IN ('2023‑01‑31','2023‑12‑31').  

Below are ten exploratory → final Snowflake SQL snippets (each limited to 20 rows) that walk from simple discovery to computing the requested percent changes.

```sql
-- 1.  Locate the GEO_ID for the Phoenix‑Mesa‑Scottsdale, AZ Metro Area
SELECT "GEO_ID","GEO_NAME","LEVEL"
FROM "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."GEOGRAPHY_INDEX"
WHERE "GEO_NAME" ILIKE '%Phoenix%Mesa%Scottsdale%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  List all counties contained in the Phoenix Metro so we can sum their IRS inflow values
SELECT "RELATED_GEO_ID" AS "COUNTY_GEO_ID",
       "RELATED_GEO_NAME"
FROM "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."GEOGRAPHY_RELATIONSHIPS"
WHERE "GEO_ID" = '<Phoenix_GEO_ID_here>'      -- replace with result from query #1
  AND "RELATIONSHIP_TYPE" = 'Contains'
  AND "RELATED_LEVEL"    = 'County'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  Discover candidate variable‑codes for gross income inflow (AGI)
SELECT DISTINCT "VARIABLE"
FROM "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."IRS_MIGRATION_BY_CHARACTERISTIC_ATTRIBUTES"
WHERE "VARIABLE" ILIKE '%Inflow%'
  AND "VARIABLE" ILIKE '%adjusted%gross%income%'
  AND "VARIABLE" ILIKE '%All_AGI_classes%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4.  Preview annual inflow AGI values for one Phoenix county in 2022‑2023
SELECT "GEO_ID","VARIABLE","DATE","VALUE","UNIT"
FROM "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."IRS_MIGRATION_BY_CHARACTERISTIC_TIMESERIES"
WHERE "GEO_ID" = '<One_County_GEO_ID>'          -- replace with county from query #2
  AND "VARIABLE" = '<Chosen_Variable_Code>'     -- replace with variable from query #3
  AND "DATE" BETWEEN '2022-12-31' AND '2023-12-31'
ORDER BY "DATE"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5.  Aggregate 2022 & 2023 inflow AGI across ALL counties in the metro
SELECT "DATE",
       SUM("VALUE") AS "METRO_INFLOW_AGI_USD"
FROM  "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."IRS_MIGRATION_BY_CHARACTERISTIC_TIMESERIES"
WHERE "GEO_ID" IN (SELECT "RELATED_GEO_ID"
                   FROM "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."GEOGRAPHY_RELATIONSHIPS"
                   WHERE "GEO_ID" = '<Phoenix_GEO_ID_here>'
                     AND "RELATIONSHIP_TYPE"='Contains'
                     AND "RELATED_LEVEL"='County')
  AND "VARIABLE" = '<Chosen_Variable_Code>'
  AND "DATE" IN ('2022-12-31','2023-12-31')
GROUP BY "DATE"
ORDER BY "DATE"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6.  Identify the variable‑code for the seasonally‑adjusted purchase‑only monthly HPI
SELECT DISTINCT "VARIABLE"
FROM "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."FHFA_HOUSE_PRICE_ATTRIBUTES"
WHERE "VARIABLE" ILIKE '%purchase-only_monthly_SA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7.  Pull monthly SA purchase‑only HPI values for the Phoenix Metro in 2023
SELECT "DATE","VALUE","UNIT"
FROM "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."FHFA_HOUSE_PRICE_TIMESERIES"
WHERE "GEO_ID"  = '<Phoenix_GEO_ID_here>'
  AND "VARIABLE" = '<HPI_Variable_Code>'       -- from query #6
  AND "DATE" BETWEEN '2023-01-31' AND '2023-12-31'
ORDER BY "DATE"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8.  Extract the first and last 2023 HPI observations (Jan & Dec)
WITH hpi AS (
  SELECT "DATE","VALUE"
  FROM "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."FHFA_HOUSE_PRICE_TIMESERIES"
  WHERE "GEO_ID"  = '<Phoenix_GEO_ID_here>'
    AND "VARIABLE" = '<HPI_Variable_Code>'
    AND "DATE" IN ('2023-01-31','2023-12-31')
)
SELECT *
FROM hpi
ORDER BY "DATE"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9.  Compute % change in SA purchase‑only HPI for 2023
WITH hpi AS (
  SELECT "DATE","VALUE"
  FROM "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."FHFA_HOUSE_PRICE_TIMESERIES"
  WHERE "GEO_ID"  = '<Phoenix_GEO_ID_here>'
    AND "VARIABLE" = '<HPI_Variable_Code>'
    AND "DATE" IN ('2023-01-31','2023-12-31')
)
SELECT (MAX(CASE WHEN "DATE"='2023-12-31' THEN "VALUE" END) -
        MAX(CASE WHEN "DATE"='2023-01-31' THEN "VALUE" END))
        /
        MAX(CASE WHEN "DATE"='2023-01-31' THEN "VALUE" END)
        * 100.0  AS "HPI_PCT_CHANGE_2023"
FROM hpi
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10.  Compute % change in gross income inflow for the metro from 2022 to 2023
WITH inflow AS (
  SELECT "DATE",
         SUM("VALUE") AS "METRO_INFLOW_AGI_USD"
  FROM  "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."IRS_MIGRATION_BY_CHARACTERISTIC_TIMESERIES"
  WHERE "GEO_ID" IN (SELECT "RELATED_GEO_ID"
                     FROM "US_REAL_ESTATE"."CYBERSYN"."GEOGRAPHY_RELATIONSHIPS"
                     WHERE "GEO_ID" = '<Phoenix_GEO_ID_here>'
                       AND "RELATIONSHIP_TYPE"='Contains'
                       AND "RELATED_LEVEL"='County')
    AND "VARIABLE" = '<Chosen_Variable_Code>'
    AND "DATE" IN ('2022-12-31','2023-12-31')
  GROUP BY "DATE"
)
SELECT (MAX(CASE WHEN "DATE"='2023-12-31' THEN "METRO_INFLOW_AGI_USD" END) -
        MAX(CASE WHEN "DATE"='2022-12-31' THEN "METRO_INFLOW_AGI_USD" END))
        /
        MAX(CASE WHEN "DATE"='2022-12-31' THEN "METRO_INFLOW_AGI_USD" END)
        * 100.0  AS "INCOME_INFLOW_PCT_CHANGE_2023"
FROM inflow
LIMIT 20;
```

